  {
    "pkheadingid": 523,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 502,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 72744,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 224,
        "headingId": 502,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>All 7&nbsp;cases reported to date were localized in the pineal region.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-05-13T12:30:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 524,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 503,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 72745,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 224,
        "headingId": 503,
        "headingText": "<p>The clinical features are similar to those of pineal parenchymal tumours&nbsp;(see under <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/45/78\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Pineocytoma</em>).</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-05-31T12:30:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 525,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 504,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 72746,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 224,
        "headingId": 504,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The median age of 4&nbsp;female and 3&nbsp;male patients was 40&nbsp;years (range: 15&ndash;61&nbsp;years) {31732806}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-05-13T12:30:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 526,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 505,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 72747,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 224,
        "headingId": 505,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-05-13T12:30:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 527,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 506,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 72748,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 224,
        "headingId": 506,
        "headingText": "\r\n<h5>Cell of origin</h5>\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n<h5>Genetic profile</h5>\r\n<p>Apart from alterations affecting the <em>SMARCB1</em> region on 22q11, chromosomal alterations are rare and non-recurrent {31732806}.</p>\r\n<p>On DNA methylation profiling, DMT, <em>SMARCB1</em>-mutant, forms a distinct group located in close proximity to one of the molecular subgroups of atypical teratoid/rhabdoid tumour (AT/RT-MYC) and to poorly differentiated chordoma {31732806}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-05-13T12:30:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 534,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 513,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 72749,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 224,
        "headingId": 513,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data available</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-05-13T12:30:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 528,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 507,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 72750,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 224,
        "headingId": 507,
        "headingText": "<p>DMT, <em>SMARCB1</em>-mutant, is characterized by an admixture of variably dense cords of small to medium-sized oval to spindled and epithelioid cells embedded in a heavily collagenized matrix. Tumour cells are dispersed to a variable extent within a loose pale basophilic myxoid matrix. Fascicular and whorling growth patterns may be encountered, and irregularly shaped and elongated blood vessels with marked fibrosis are frequent. Scattered rhabdoid tumour cells are rare. Mitotic activity is exceptional (&lt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;mitosis/mm<sup>2</sup>) {31732806}</p>\r\n<h5>Grading</h5>\r\n<p>The biological behaviour of DMT, <em>SMARCB1</em>-mutant, seems to be less aggressive than that of atypical teratoid/rhabdoid tumour {31732806}, but grading remains to be defined.</p>\r\n<h5>Proliferation</h5>\r\n<p>The Ki-67 (MIB1) proliferation index is low (median: 3%), and only one tumour in a young patient showed higher proliferative activity (15%) {31732806}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunophenotype</h5>\r\n<p>Tumour cells show loss of nuclear SMARCB1 (INI1) expression. Expression of CD34 and EMA is often present {31732806}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-05-18T17:50:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 529,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
